block content
    h1 Obstructed defecation syndrome
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22089-obstructed-defecation") Cleveland Clinic]:
    blockquote Obstructed defecation syndrome (ODS) is a functional pooping disorder. People with ODS have trouble evacuating their bowels, resulting in constipation. It may be for a variety of reasons, both mechanical and psychological. Treatment is usually conservative and holistic, but sometimes surgery is needed.
